computing/INSTALL

========================================
2021 Notes

0) Fresh Ubuntu 20 install, from scratch.  Fresh TeX Live, from the web install.

1) To get Asymptote to run:
  a) need to install libglut.
  b) need to install imagemagick
  c) In /etc/ImageMagick-6/policy.xml needed to change lines about PS, PDF, etc
  from rights="none" to rights="read|write".
  d) Put these lines at the end of your .profile in your home directory,
  (you need to change "/Documents/computing" to wherever you put the repo):

# Directories for the Asymptote drawing program
export ASYMPTOTE_DIR=$HOME/Documents/computing/src/asy:$HOME/Documents/computing/src/asy/share:$HOME/Documents/computing/src/asy/asy-graphtheory-master/modules:$ASYMPTOTE_DIR

  Log out and log in again (this runs the profile).  Check that it all works
  by opening a terminal and running "echo $ASYMPTOTE_DIR".
  e) Comment: there is an issue between Asymptote and Ghostscript.  There
  was some kind of vulnerability in GS, and they made some changes, and
  the Asy version does not work with the GS version.  I am sure that this
  will all work out someday, but as of today (2021-June-08) it can't
  make the 3d.asy file without by-hand compilation of at least one of the
  two programs.  I instead added a number of files, such as
  src/background/asy/3d/3d000.pdf to the repo as a temp patch.


  